  "term": "victimization",
  "definition": "In this source, victimization refers to being harmed by fraud or scams, involving deception, emotional manipulation, and a sense of betrayal, not just financial loss. It is linked to lasting psychosocial and mental health effects such as anxiety, depression, shame, self-blame, reduced trust, and lower quality of life.",
